  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f095fd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3836,
      "bookHadithIndex": 101,
      "text": "Narrated Aisha, Ummul Mu'minin: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to eat melon with fresh dates, and he used to say: The heat of the one is broken by the coolness of the other, and the coolness of the one by the heat of the other",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3836-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3836-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3836-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f095fe",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3837,
      "bookHadithIndex": 102,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn Busr ibn Atiyyah ibn Busr: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to visit us and we offered him butter and dates, for he liked butter and dates",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3837-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3837-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3837-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f095ff",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3838,
      "bookHadithIndex": 103,
      "text": "Narrated Jabir ibn Abdullah: I was on an expedition along with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). We got the vessels and skins of the polytheists and used them. But he did not object to them (i.e. us) for that (action)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3838-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3838-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3838-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09600",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3839,
      "bookHadithIndex": 104,
      "text": "Abu Tha’labah al-khushani said that he asked the Messenger of Allah(ﷺ):We live in the neighbourhood of the People of the Book and they cook in their pots(the flesh of) swine and drink wine in their vessels. The Messenger of Allah(ﷺ) said: If you find any other pots, then eat in them and drink. But if you do not find any others, then wash them with water and eat and drink (In them)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3839-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3839-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3839-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09601",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3840,
      "bookHadithIndex": 105,
      "text": "Jabir said:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent us on an expedition and made Abu ‘Ubaidah b. al-Jarrah our leader. We had to meet a caravan of the Quraish. He gave us a bag of dates as a light meal during the journey. We had nothing except that. Abu ‘Ubaidah would give each of us one date. We used to suck them as a child sucks, and drink water after that and it sufficed us that day till night. We used to beat leaves off the trees with our sticks (for food), wetted them with water and ate them. We then went to the coast of the sea. There appeared to us a body like a great mound. When we came to it, we found that it was an animal called al-anbar. Abu ‘Ubaidah said: It is a carrion, and it is not lawful for us. He then said: No, we are the Messengers of the Apostel of Allah (ﷺ) and we are in the path of Allah. If you are forced by necessity (to eat it), then eat it. We stayed feeding on it for one mouth, till we became fat, and we were three hundred in number. When we came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), we mentioned it to him. He said : It is a provision which Allah has brought forth for you, and give us some to eat if you have any meat of it with you. So we sent some of it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he ate (it)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3840-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3840-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3840-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3840-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (2483) Sahih Muslim (1935)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09602",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3841,
      "bookHadithIndex": 106,
      "text": "Maimunah said:A mouse fell into clarified butter. The Prophet (ﷺ) was informed of it. He said: Throw what is around it and eat",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3841-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3841-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3841-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3841-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5538)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09603",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3842,
      "bookHadithIndex": 107,
      "text": "Narrated AbuHurayrah: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: When a mouse falls into clarified butter, if it is sold, throw the mouse and what is around it away, but if it is in a liquid state, do not go near it. Al-Hasan said: AbdurRazzaq said: This tradition has been transmitted by Ma'mar, from az-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, from the Prophet (ﷺ)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3842-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3842-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09604",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3843,
      "bookHadithIndex": 108,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn Abbas: The tradition mentioned above (No. 3833) has also been transmitted by Ibn Abbas from Maymunah, from the Prophet (ﷺ) like the tradition narrated by az-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3843-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Shadh"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3843-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09605",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3844,
      "bookHadithIndex": 109,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah reported the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying:when a fly alights in anyone’s vessel, he should plunge it all in, for in one of its wings there is a disease, and in the other is a cure. It prevents the wing of it is which there is a cure, so plunge it all in (the vessel)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3844-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3844-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3844-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3844-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09606",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3845,
      "bookHadithIndex": 110,
      "text": "Anas b. Malik said that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ate food, he licked his three fingers. And he said:If the morsel of one of you falls down, he should wipe away anything injurious on it and eat it and not leave it for the devil. And he ordered us to clean the dish, for one of you does not leave it for the devil. And he ordered us to clean the dish, for one of you does not know in what part of his food the blessing lies",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3845-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3845-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3845-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3845-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim (2034)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09607",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3846,
      "bookHadithIndex": 111,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah reported the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying :If the servant of any of you prepares food for him, and he brings it to him, while he had suffered its heat and smoke. He should make him sit with him to eat. If the food is scanty, he should put one or two morsels in his hand",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3846-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3846-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3846-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3846-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (2557) Sahih Muslim (1663)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09608",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3847,
      "bookHadithIndex": 112,
      "text": "Ibn ‘Abbas reported the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying :When one of you eats, he must not wipe his hand with a handkerchief till he licks it or gives it to someone to lick",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3847-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3847-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3847-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3847-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5456) Sahih Muslim (2031)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09609",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3848,
      "bookHadithIndex": 113,
      "text": "Ka’b b. Malik said:The Prophet (ﷺ) used to eat with three fingers and not wipe his before licking it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3848-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3848-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3848-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3848-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim (2032)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0960a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3849,
      "bookHadithIndex": 114,
      "text": "Abu Umamah said:When the food cloth was removed, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “praise be to Allah abundantly and sincerely, of such a nature as is productive of blessing, is not insufficient, Abandoned, or ignored, O our lord.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3849-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3849-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3849-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3849-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5458)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0960b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3850,
      "bookHadithIndex": 115,
      "text": "Narrated AbuSa'id al-Khudri: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) finished his food, he said: \"Praise be to Allah Who has given us food and drink and made us Muslims",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3850-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3850-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3850-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3850-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0960c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3851,
      "bookHadithIndex": 116,
      "text": "Narrated AbuAyyub al-Ansari: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ate or drank, he said: \"Praise be to Allah Who has given food and drink and made it easy to swallow, and provided an exit for it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3851-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3851-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3851-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3851-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0960d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3852,
      "bookHadithIndex": 117,
      "text": "Narrated AbuHurayrah: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: If anyone spends the night with grease on his hand which he has not washed away, he can blame only himself if some trouble comes to him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3852-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3852-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3852-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3852-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0960e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 28,
      "hadithIndex": 3853,
      "bookHadithIndex": 118,
      "text": "Narrated Jabir ibn Abdullah: AbulHaytham ibn at-Tayhan prepared food for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he invited the Prophet (ﷺ) and his Companions. When they finished (food), the said: If some people enter the house of a man, his food is eaten and his drink is drunk, and they supplicate (to Allah) for him, this is his reward",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3853-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3853-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3853-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-28-3853-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0960f",
